    title: "France calls Israel’s entry ban on left-wing leader ‘demagogic’",
    summary: "France calls Israel’s entry ban on left-wing leader ‘demagogic’ French Foreign Minister Jean-Noel Barrot condemned Israel’s decision to bar left-wing officials, including Jean-Luc Melenchon, leader of the La France Insoumise party, from entering the country in a post on X on Thursday. \"This demagogic decision, coming from a government that has repeatedly violated international law, plays into the hands of those who, like La France Insoumise, make a living out of exploiting the Israeli-Palestinian conflict,\" Barrot wrote. \"France will continue tirelessly to work toward a two-state solution and peaceful coexistence between the Israeli and Palestinian peoples.\" Le gouvernement d'affaires courantes de Benyamin Netanyahou vient d'interdire l'accès à son territoire à des responsables de la France insoumise. Cette décision démagogique, émanant d'un gouvernement qui a multiplié les violations du droit international, fait le jeu de ceux qui, comme La France insoumise, vivent de l'instrumentalisation du conflit israélo-palestinien. La France continuera inlassablement à agir pour la solution à deux États et la coexistence pacifique des peuples israélien et palestinien. — Jean-Noël Barrot (@jnbarrot) November 12, 2026",
    preview: "France calls Israel’s entry ban on left-wing leader ‘demagogic’ French Foreign Minister Jean-Noel Barrot condemned Israel’s decision to bar left-wing officials, including Jean-Luc Melenchon, leader of the La France Insoumise party, from entering the country in a post on X on Thursday. \"This demagogic decision, coming from a government that has repeatedly violated international law, plays into the hands of those who, like La France Insoumise, make a living out of exploiting the Israeli-Palestinian conflict,\" Barrot wrote.",
    body: "France calls Israel’s entry ban on left-wing leader ‘demagogic’ French Foreign Minister Jean-Noel Barrot condemned Israel’s decision to bar left-wing officials, including Jean-Luc Melenchon, leader of the La France Insoumise party, from entering the country in a post on X on Thursday. \"This demagogic decision, coming from a government that has repeatedly violated international law, plays into the hands of those who, like La France Insoumise, make a living out of exploiting the Israeli-Palestinian conflict,\" Barrot wrote.\n\n\"France will continue tirelessly to work toward a two-state solution and peaceful coexistence between the Israeli and Palestinian peoples.\" Le gouvernement d'affaires courantes de Benyamin Netanyahou vient d'interdire l'accès à son territoire à des responsables de la France insoumise. Cette décision démagogique, émanant d'un gouvernement qui a multiplié les violations du droit international, fait le jeu de ceux qui, comme La France insoumise, vivent de l'instrumentalisation du conflit israélo-palestinien.\n\nLa France continuera inlassablement à agir pour la solution à deux États et la coexistence pacifique des peuples israélien et palestinien. — Jean-Noël Barrot (@jnbarrot) November 12, 2026",
